Package: optical2digital
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kyle Mikolajczyk <kyle@kylem.org>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/kylemikableh/Optical2Digital
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libgl1, libglib2.0-0, libnss3, libnspr4,
 libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3, libexpat1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1,
 libxcb1, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1,
 libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xinerama0,
 libxcb-xkb1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2,
 libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxext6, libxrender1, libxtst6, libdrm2,
 libgbm1, libcups2, libminizip1 | libminizip1t64, libasound2 | libasound2t64
Description: Optical film audio to digital PCM converter
 Extracts and converts variable-area / variable-density optical soundtracks
 from motion-picture film scans (image sequences or video) into digital PCM
 audio, through a native desktop UI. The application bundles its own Python
 runtime, web frontend, and a static ffmpeg, so nothing else needs to be
 installed for it to run.
